odeVoice","code":"SortComparator"},{"type":"text","text":" is provided to aid in comparing or sorting "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftTimecodeCore\/documentation\/SwiftTimecodeCore\/Timecode"},{"text":" instances.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Neighboring instances of identical timecode are considered sorted.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Timeline length and wrap point is determined by the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftTimecodeCore\/documentation\/SwiftTimecodeCore\/Timecode\/upperLimit-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property. The timeline is considered linear for 24 hours (or 100 days) from this start time,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrapping around the upper limit.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Working-with-a-Non-Zero-Timeline-Start","text":"Working with a Non-Zero Timeline Start","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sometimes a timeline does not have a zero start time (00:00:00:00). For example, many DAW"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"software applications such as Pro Tools allows a project start time to be set to any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"timecode. Its timeline then extends for 24 hours from that timecode, wrapping around over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"00:00:00:00 at some point along the timeline."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Methods to sort and test sort order of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftTimecodeCore\/documentation\/SwiftTimecodeCore\/Timecode","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" collections are provided.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, given a 24 hour limit:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A timeline start of 